372 - How Beauteous Are Their Feet
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 372
Topic: Christian Church - 

Verse 1:
[F]How beauteous are [Dm]their feet [F]Who stand on Zion's hill;
[F]Who [C]bring salvation on their [F]tongues, [Am]And [Bb]words of peace [F/C]reveal!

Verse 2:
[F]How charming [C]is [F]their voice,
[F]So sweet [Dm]the [C]tidings [F]are:
[F]"Zion, [C/E]behold [F]thy [C]Savior [F/C]King;
[F]He reigns [C/E]and [Am]triumphs [Bb]here!"

Verse 3:
[F]How happy [C]are [F]our ears,
[F]That hear [Dm]the [C]joyful [F]sound
[F]Which [C/E]kings [F/A]and [C/E]prophets [Am]waited [F/C]for,
[F]And [C/E]sought, but [Dm]never [F/C]found!

Verse 4:
[F]How blessed [Dm]are [F]our eyes,
[F]That see this [Dm]heavenly [F]light;
[F]Prophets and [C/E]kings [Dm]desired [Bb]it [F/C]long,
[F]But [C/E]died without [Bb]the [F/C]sight!

Verse 5:
[F]The watchmen [C]join [F]their voice,
[F]And tuneful [C]notes [F/A]employ;
[F]Jerusalem [Dm]breaks [Am]forth [Bb]in [F/C]songs,
[F]And [C/E]deserts [Dm]learn [Bb]the [F/C]joy.
